# Traverxec sanitized evidence index

Source: /home/kali/Platforms/HackTheBox/Traverxec
Target: $BoxIP
Platform: HackTheBox
Operating system: Debian 10 x86_64

Open TCP services:
- 22/tcp SSH, OpenSSH 7.9p1 Debian 10
- 80/tcp HTTP, Nostromo 1.9.6

Initial access:
- Nostromo CVE-2019-16278
- Exploit-DB 47837
- RCE confirmed as www-data

Configuration findings:
- /var/nostromo/conf/nhttpd.conf disclosed the Basic-auth file and home-directory mapping
- Home directories were published through public_www
- A protected SSH archive was reachable under the $Username home path

Credential path:
- The htpasswd record was extracted through RCE and cracked offline
- Basic authentication downloaded the SSH archive
- The encrypted RSA key was converted with ssh2john and cracked offline
- Credential values and key material remain private

Privilege escalation:
- SSH foothold as $Username
- /home/$Username/bin/server-stats.sh invoked the exact permitted sudo command
- sudo -n /usr/bin/journalctl -n5 -unostromo.service opened a pager
- !/bin/bash from the pager produced a root shell

Proof and closeout:
- User and root proof were collected privately
- High-thread Gobuster caused temporary connection refusals; reduced concurrency was required
- The public exploit copy needed a stray-line syntax repair
- Generic journalctl sudo invocation was denied because the sudo rule was argument-specific
- boxdone was recorded in the supplied command log
- No persistent target-side files were created
